{UTF-8}
Sun= 200
	~	Dmnl
	~	No solar/irradiance dataset was in your file, so this stays a constant \
		placeholder for the diagram node. Water Temperature below is now \
		calibrated directly from the real IGKB measurements instead of being \
		derived from Sun.
	|

Water Temperature= 8.5+0.057*(Time-1945)
	~	Celsius
	~	Linear fit to the real IGKB chart: about 8.5C in 1945 rising to about \
		12.5C by 2015 (the chart's data runs 1945-2015). This matches your note \
		that 1990-2017 averaged 1.2C warmer than the prior three decades.
	|

Evaporation= 0.01*Water Temperature
	~	m/Year
	~	Unchanged mechanism; still a dead end per the diagram.
	|

External Migratory Animals=2
	~	Ton/Year
	~	No data was provided for this node.
	|

Agriculture with Fertilizer=5+80*EXP(-((Time-1977)/15)*((Time-1977)/15))
	~	Ton/Year
	~	Reshaped into a rise-then-fall curve fit to the real total-phosphorus \
		chart: low before 1960, peaking around 1975-1980, and then declining.
	|

Pollution Microplastic=MAX(0,MIN(1,0.008*(Time-1975)+0.1))
	~	Dmnl
	~	CHANGE INTO GENERAL POLLUTION? No microplastic dataset. Used the real \
		chloride trend instead (rising steadily from about 4 to 7.5 mg/L, \
		1975-2020, attributed to road salt) as the best available proxy for \
		general pollution pressure, rescaled onto the model's existing 0-1 \
		severity scale.
	|

Food= (0.02+0.08*EXP(-((Time-1978)/20)*((Time-1978)/20)))*MAX(0,1-Pollution Microplastic\
		*0.5)*IF THEN ELSE(Time>=2024,0,1)
	~	1/Year
	~	Reshaped to track the real catch data: fishing pressure rising through the \
		productive decades (catches peaked around 1970-1990), declining after, \
		still reduced somewhat by Pollution Microplastic as before, and forced to \
		exactly 0 from 2024 onward because whitefish fishing in Lake Constance has \
		been banned since 2024 (per IGKB).
	|

O2 Levels= INTEG ((8-0.3*(Water Temperature-9)-0.04*Nutrient Levels-O2 Levels)*0.3,
		6.8)
	~	mg/L
	~	Units switched to mg/L to match the real oxygen chart and the 6 mg/L \
		threshold the source calls critical for whitefish eggs and deep-water \
		life. Relaxes toward a target set by Water Temperature (capturing both \
		lower O2 solubility and the weaker winter circulation your source \
		describes: 'water circulation is decreasing because of milder winters and \
		higher water temperatures') and by Nutrient Levels (the same \
		eutrophication-to-hypoxia link the O2 and phosphorus charts show together).
	|

Plants= INTEG ((2*Nutrient Levels+5*External Migratory Animals-Plants)*0.5,
		20)
	~	Ton
	~	Unchanged mechanism (relaxes toward a level set by Nutrient Levels and \
		External Migratory Animals); no plant-biomass data available, so this \
		remains an abstracted proxy stock.
	|

Nutrient Levels= INTEG (
	(Agriculture with Fertilizer+0.05*Plants+0.02*Fish Stock-Nutrient Levels)*0.4,
		6)
	~	Ton
	~	Relaxes toward Agriculture with Fertilizer (now the real P curve) plus \
		small Plant/Fish contributions, with a response time of about 2.5 years so \
		it tracks the real phosphorus curve's rise and fall rather than drifting \
		away from it.
	|

Fish Stock= INTEG (0.35*Fish Stock*(1-Fish Stock/1500)*(Plants/(Plants+100))*(O2 Levels\
		/(O2 Levels+3))-Food*Fish Stock-0.02*Fish Stock,
		300)
	~	Ton
	~	Initial value and scale set to the order of magnitude of the real \
		professional catch data (roughly 200-1900 t/a, 1914-2025). Growth now \
		depends on Plants (food) and O2 Levels (health) as before, with Food \
		removing stock through harvest. Fish Stock here approximates standing \
		population biomass, not annual catch, so it will not match the real chart \
		point-for-point even where well calibrated.
	|

FINAL TIME  = 2030
	~	Year
	~	The final time for the simulation (extends a few years past the last real \
		data point to show the post-2024 fishing-ban trajectory).
	|

INITIAL TIME  = 1945
	~	Year
	~	The initial time for the simulation, matching the start of the real \
		water-temperature record.
	|

SAVEPER  = 
        1
	~	Year [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored (annual, matching the real \
		data's resolution).
	|

TIME STEP  = 0.1
	~	Year [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation (finer than SAVEPER for numerical \
		accuracy).
	|

\\\---/// Sketch information - do not modify anything except names
